# The repository root ignores *.png as build output. The files under this
# directory are the opposite: committed REFERENCE ASSETS, copied from the
# legacy Venice tree so that a golden run's initial condition and its one
# surviving design artifact travel with this repository and cannot drift when a
# sibling checkout moves. Without this negation the initial image is silently
# absent from a fresh clone and the Venice parity harness fails on a machine
# that never had the Venice repo.
#
# `results/.../0_final-*.jpg` needs no negation only because the root ignores
# no JPEG pattern today. It is load-bearing in exactly the same way -- it is
# the sole non-scalar record of the reference run's geometry -- so anything
# added to the root ignore file must keep it tracked.
!*.png
